### 11. AUTOMATED GRADING AND CALCULATION ENGINE

Develop a configurable grading engine.

Features:
- Automatic assessment total calculation.
- Weighted score calculation.
- Subject total calculation.
- Subject average calculation.
- Overall student average.
- Grade assignment.
- Performance descriptions.
- Aggregate calculation where applicable.
- Class ranking where enabled.
- Tie handling.
- Missing assessment handling.
- Absent and exempted status handling.
- Automatic recalculation after authorised changes.

Allow administrators to configure grading boundaries.

Example configuration:

80–100 = A – Excellent
70–79 = B – Very Good
60–69 = C – Good
50–59 = D – Fair
0–49 = E – Needs Improvement

These are illustrative values only.

Never hardcode them.

The system must allow different grading scales for different examination levels.

Use database transactions and consistent calculation rules.

Ensure all calculations are reproducible and tested.

### 12. RESULTS VERIFICATION AND APPROVAL

Implement a controlled examination approval workflow:

Subject Teacher → DOS → Head Teacher → Published Results.

Features:
- Teachers submit completed marks.
- DOS receives submission notifications.
- DOS reviews submitted marks.
- DOS returns incorrect marks for correction.
- DOS verifies subject results.
- Head Teacher performs final approval where required.
- Approved results are locked.
- Published results become available to authorised recipients.
- Corrections to approved results require explicit authorisation and a recorded reason.
- Maintain a complete version history.

Display approval progress using a clean workflow tracker.

Never allow an unauthorised user to bypass the approval process.

